## 1. System Role in the Platform

The marketing site is not where USRad gets its brand in front of people. It is where USRad closes the gap between a person with a medical need and the platform that serves it — and simultaneously where the platform recruits the supply that makes serving that need possible.

It is the entry layer of the entire business. Every patient who books an MRI, every imaging center that joins the network, and every employer who signs an enterprise agreement begins their relationship with USRad here. The platform downstream — the booking engine, the provider portal, the payment system — only generates revenue if this system delivers the right person to the right entry point at the right moment.

It feeds three distinct downstream systems, each with a different economic model:

The **Patient Booking System** is the primary revenue engine. Every patient who completes a search on the homepage and arrives at the Remix booking flow is a potential per-scan transaction. The marketing site's job in this pipeline is to get a qualified patient to that handoff point with enough price transparency and procedural clarity that they complete the booking without hesitation.

The **Provider Network** is the supply engine. Without contracted imaging centers, there are no results for patients to choose from. The marketing site's provider acquisition funnel — the landing page, the network map, the SmartMatch explainer, the portal tour — is the top of a pipeline that ends with a signed Provider Services Agreement and an active facility in the network. Every new provider who joins through this system expands USRad's geographic coverage and increases the probability of a patient finding a qualified result in their market.

The **Employer Pipeline** is the B2B engine. Enterprise employers represent contracted volume — a single employer agreement can generate dozens of bookings per month. The employer funnel's job is to capture a qualified business lead, provide enough evidence of ROI to warrant an executive conversation, and route that lead to a scheduled consultation.

The marketing site is the only system in the USRad platform that simultaneously serves all three of these pipelines. Its health directly determines the growth rate of the entire business.

