## 6. Portal Tour — Pre-Sales System

The portal tour page answers the question every serious provider asks before committing to a new business relationship: "What am I actually signing up for?"

The page is structured as a scrollable walkthrough of the real provider experience — application, credentialing, patient reception, and payment — with authentic detail drawn from the actual platform engineering. The onboarding steps it describes match the real onboarding flow. The Go-Live Requirements panel it shows matches the real provider portal dashboard. The terminology it uses matches the platform's own terminology layer.

This authenticity is the page's primary conversion mechanism. A provider who reaches the portal tour and scrolls through all four steps has, in effect, previewed the product. They know what the application form asks for. They know the credentialing timeline. They know how patients arrive and what privacy controls are in place. They know what the payment process looks like. When they click "Begin Provider Onboarding," they are not making a leap of faith. They are confirming a decision they have already effectively made.

The strategic value of this approach is that it moves objection resolution from the sales process to the marketing system. A provider who would have had questions about the onboarding process, the patient privacy model, or the payment timeline has those questions answered before they ever speak to a USRad representative. This reduces the burden on any human sales or support function and increases the conversion rate of providers who reach the signup page.

The portal tour also functions as a quality filter. A provider who reads the full walkthrough and still applies is a provider who understands what the commitment involves. They are less likely to drop off during credentialing, less likely to be surprised by the platform's requirements, and more likely to become a high-performing network partner.

