## 7. Employer Acquisition Engine

The employer funnel operates on a longer sales cycle than either the patient or provider funnels, and its architecture reflects this reality. It is not designed to convert on a single visit. It is designed to qualify, score, and route high-value leads toward a scheduled consultation.

### Funnel Structure

The employer landing page establishes the value proposition with surgical precision: hospital MRI costs $3,200; USRad costs $420; here is a composite case study showing a mid-size employer reducing imaging spend from $3.3 million to $1.8 million annually while cutting turnaround time by 18 days. This is not aspirational messaging. It is a business case delivered in the first scroll.

The ROI calculator converts the abstract value proposition into a company-specific number. An HR director entering their employee count and estimated imaging volume receives a personalized savings projection — a tangible figure they can take to a budget conversation. The ROI report generator takes this further: it produces a PDF with the company's specific numbers, branded and formatted for executive review. This artifact can be shared in a leadership meeting without the USRad team being in the room.

The gated implementation guide — requiring a work email address, rejecting free email domains, and blocking submissions that arrive in under three seconds — is a lead quality filter. A person who provides their work email and downloads a 30-day implementation timeline is expressing qualified intent. The system records this as a 20-point intent score increase in Supabase. A lead that then schedules a consultation has accumulated multiple intent signals across multiple visits — the scoring layer creates a prioritized lead queue without any manual qualification work.

### Conversion Logic

The employer funnel is designed for a buying committee dynamic. The person who downloads the implementation guide may not be the person who signs the contract. The ROI calculator output can be shared. The case study can be forwarded. Each piece of content is designed to travel through an organization independently, building the internal case for USRad before the sales conversation begins. This is B2B demand generation functioning correctly.

