## 10. System Weaknesses

### HIGH · No Sitemap or Robots File — 15+ Months Unfixed

This is the most consequential unfixed issue in the system. Without a sitemap, search engine crawlers must discover pages through link traversal — a process that is both slower and less reliable than directed crawling. More critically, without a robots file, test pages, debug API endpoints, provider portal pages, and administrative interfaces are indexable. A search engine that indexes these pages wastes crawl budget, may expose internal data in search results, and will not correctly prioritize the high-value marketing pages that generate patient and provider traffic. This is a foundational SEO gap that has been flagged since the first audit and remains unresolved.

**Business consequence:** Every week without a sitemap is a week of delayed search engine discovery for new pages. The three new provider pages — network map, SmartMatch, portal tour — may not be indexed for weeks or months after launch. Provider traffic that should be arriving organically is not.

### HIGH · Header/Footer Sync Is 15+ Months Stale

The CarbonHeader and CarbonFooter on the marketing site must match the equivalent header and footer in the Remix application. They last synced in December 2025. Any navigation changes, link additions, or login URL updates made in the Remix application since then are not reflected in the marketing site — and vice versa. A patient who navigates from the Remix booking flow back to the marketing site, or from the marketing site into Remix, encounters potentially different navigation. This is not a minor visual inconsistency — it erodes the impression that these are parts of a single, coherent platform.

**Business consequence:** Every navigation change in one application creates drift in the other. This gap compounds over time and becomes progressively more expensive to resolve.

### HIGH · Debug APIs in Production Expose Internal Data

Three API endpoints — `/api/debug-data`, `/api/debug-facilities`, and `/api/test` — are accessible in the production environment without authentication. These endpoints expose internal facility and platform data to anyone who knows or can discover the URL. This is a security exposure that creates competitive intelligence risk, potential data privacy issues, and audit liability.

**Business consequence:** Competitor scraping, unauthorized access to facility data, and potential HIPAA-adjacent exposure if patient-related data is accessible through these endpoints.

### MEDIUM · Dual Provider Funnel Dilutes Authority and Confuses Audience

Two separate provider acquisition funnels — the `/provider` family and the `/imaging-center` family — target the same audience with different design languages, different copy strategies, and different conversion paths. This creates internal competition for SEO authority on provider-related queries, splits conversion data across two pipelines, and requires maintaining two sets of pages that serve the same purpose.

**Business consequence:** SEO authority for "imaging center partnership" and related queries is split across two URL structures. Neither funnel is as authoritative as a unified funnel would be. Provider prospects who encounter both may perceive brand inconsistency.

### MEDIUM · Static Fake Data on the Provider Teaser

The `MarketOpportunityTeaser` component on the provider landing page shows "5 USRad partners" and "520 MRI centers mapped" as static numbers. These do not reflect the live network. A provider who sees these numbers on the landing page and then explores the network map — which shows the real, live network data — will notice the discrepancy. In a context where the entire provider funnel is designed around credibility and transparency, showing fake numbers on the entry page is a meaningful trust risk.

### MEDIUM · Non-Functional Chat Widget on Every Page

The "Need help?" chat bubble appears in the bottom right of every CarbonLayout page. It has no backend. It does nothing when clicked. This is worse than not having a chat widget — it actively signals to patients and providers that the platform's support infrastructure is cosmetic.

### LOW · Global Lottie Load on Every Page

Roughly 250KB of animation library is loaded on every CarbonLayout page, including pages that use no animations. This is a performance tax paid by every visitor to every marketing page. On mobile devices with slower connections, this is a meaningful contributor to slow page load times that directly affects conversion rates.

